            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Considering that `tT` work but `fF` don't and that you mapped plain `s` to `surround.add`, I would guess that you type `sf` and `sF` somewhat fast. These leads to activating `find` and `find_left` default mappings, which find surrounding character (not really a default `f/F` motions). To verify that, first type `s`, then wait some time (at least `timeoutlen` milliseconds) and only then try `f/F`.\r\n\r\nThere are several solutions for your:\r\n- Don't create other default 'mini.surround' maps. You can supply `''` to disable them.\r\n- By aware that you need to wait after `s` before applying `f`/`F`/`h`/`n` in operator pending mode.\r\n- Decrease `timeoutlen` (seems a bit drastic, but an option nevertheless).",
